  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scgpt (config_009, acc=0.530, F1=0.515) slightly outperforms multimodal with scgpt+resnet50 weighted fusion (config_008, acc=0.525, F1=0.498), while image-only with resnet50 (config_001) is very weak (acc=0.328). This raises the critical question of whether the image modality has any useful signal or whether resnet50 is simply too weak to contribute. Question: config_007 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) is the minimal-change extension of config_008, swapping only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l. This isolates the effect of image encoder quality on multimodal performance. Why best next experiment: If imagenet_vit_l substantially improves multimodal accuracy over both config_008 and config_009, it confirms the image modality carries useful information that was being lost by a weak encoder, justifying further investment in multimodal designs. If it does not help, it strongly suggests the image channel is not contributing and the budget should focus on RNA-side improvements (encoder choice, aggregation, profile setting). This single experiment resolves a high-uncertainty, high-impact design decision before spending budget on more complex multimodal variants."
}

